<title>DUBAI: Saudi in water pipeline deal with Italy consortium.</title>
<headline>Saudi in water pipeline deal with Italy consortium.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Arabia on Wednesday</p>
<p>awarded a $223.5 million deal to a consortium of Italian companies Saipem SpA and Snamprogetti for a system to supply water to the cities of Jeddah, Mecca and Taif.</p>
<p>The official Saudi Press Agency (SPA) said Agriculture and Water Resources Minister Abdullah bin Abdul-Aziz bin Muammar signed the deal to execute a water pipeline project to the cities from a desalination plant in Shuaiba.</p>
<p>Snamprogetti is a unit of the Italian energy giant ENI .</p>
